Description: PostGIS tiger geocoder and reverse geocoder
 postgis_tiger_geocoder is a PostgreSQL extension that provides a complete
 geocoding stack for United States addresses, built on top of PostGIS and the
 U.S. Census Bureau's TIGER/Line shapefiles. The extension loads TIGER/Line
 data (such as 2025 vintages) into a normalized schema and exposes loader,
 normalization, and geocoding functions that turn street addresses into
 geographic coordinates and structured locations.
